{
  "$comment": [
    "The change manager authorizes tier 3 changes and emergencies, with a combined group for a tier 3 emergency. The change board decides exceptions about a change (document 28, issues 2 and 4).",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 4): one configuration admin accepts a configuration change on one card, and that person may be the admin who instructed it. Regulated and the strict separation overlay require a second admin through a separation rule.",
    "Aligned with the process documents (document 21, B21-9). Tier: the platform admin, and at tier 3 the platform admin and the security reviewer (P02). Data use at tier 3: the data owner and the security reviewer, because restricted data is a tier 3 answer and approval rules have no data scope yet (P02; the data taxonomy later scopes it by classification). Ownership: each proposed owner by name, and the business owner, or the sponsor and then the portfolio's accountable person when the business owner leaves or is missing (P08). Intake and autonomy level get their consultation cards (P01 step 5, P02). Retirement complete is first to respond (P09). The AI lead decides on a flagged agent (P06, P08).",
    "Intake keeps no counting rule, so the lowest-tier intake stays on the locked engine acceptance list and every other intake goes to the platform admin on the accountable card (P01 step 6)."
  ],
